Version 4
SHEET 1 880 680
WIRE -32 96 -32 64
WIRE -32 64 96 64
WIRE 176 64 224 64
FLAG -32 64 in
FLAG 224 64 out
FLAG -32 176 0
FLAG 224 128 0
SYMBOL voltage -32 80 R0
SYMATTR InstName V1
SYMATTR Value PULSE(0 {vdd} 0 1n 1n 5u 10u)
SYMBOL res 80 80 R270
SYMATTR InstName R1
SYMATTR Value 1k
SYMBOL cap 208 64 R0
SYMATTR InstName C1
SYMATTR Value 1n
TEXT -32 240 Left 2 !.param vdd=1
TEXT -32 264 Left 2 !.tran 0 30u
TEXT -32 296 Left 2 !.meas tran tdelay TRIG V(in) VAL=0.5*vdd RISE=2 TARG V(out) VAL=0.5*vdd RISE=2
TEXT -32 320 Left 2 !.meas tran trise TRIG V(out) VAL=0.1*vdd RISE=2 TARG V(out) VAL=0.9*vdd RISE=2
TEXT -32 344 Left 2 !.meas tran ratio PARAM trise/tdelay
TEXT -32 368 Left 2 !.meas tran pr AVG V(in,out)*I(R1)
TEXT -32 408 Left 2 ;Timing of an RC low-pass (tau = R1 C1 = 1 us), measured in LTspice's .MEAS syntax:
TEXT -32 432 Left 2 ;the 50 % delay (0.69 tau), the 10-90 % rise time (2.2 tau), their ratio (PARAM) and the
TEXT -32 456 Left 2 ;average power in R1. The results are listed with the plot. Check them with cursors:
TEXT -32 480 Left 2 ;click and shift-click set A and B; the readout gives the difference, and average, RMS
TEXT -32 504 Left 2 ;and integral between them. Add trace 0.5 draws a reference line at half the step.
